// Exists to be built with --freestanding, not run.
//
// ossl_shim.c is compiled with -ffreestanding -DVT_NO_LIBC like every package
// shim (src/main.c splices the flags into every package's compile line, not
// just the runtime's), so without its stub arm the <openssl/ssl.h> include
// would break the build of any program that merely imports vyto/crypto/openssl.
//
// Nothing else exercises this. The freestanding suite otherwise builds
// 01_hello.vt, which imports nothing, and every TLS test needs a socket and a
// libc — so the arm can only rot silently. That is what this fixture is for,
// exactly as tests/fixtures/mmap_freestanding.vt is for vyto/mmap's.
//
// The stub arm answers 0 / null everywhere, so ossl_available() is false and
// tls_client() returns a context whose ok() is false. The Vyto side needs no
// platform conditional to cope with that: "OpenSSL is not available" is already
// one of the outcomes every caller has to handle.
import { ossl_available, tls_client } from "vyto/crypto/openssl";

fn main() {
    if (!ossl_available()) {
        print("no OpenSSL on this target");
        return;
    }
    let c = tls_client();
    print("client context: " + str(c.ok()));
}
